WEBVTT

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.190
CP, this is 01 at OP1.

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:04.530
Monitoring situation.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:08.780
CP, this is 01. We hear footsteps, possibly Godzilla's,

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.370
but no visuals due to low visibility. Awaiting command.

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:14.770
CP, roger that. Retreat.

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:18.330
CP! This is 03. There's a huge creature flying over the city!

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:21.000
CP to 03. What is it?

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.170
No visuals through red dust.
There are huge blasts of wind!

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:26.300
This is 01.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.670
Godzilla spotted.

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:27.670
Did it see it?

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:29.010
No—I don't think so.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:35.100
Flying from Ginza towards Yurakucho...

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.040
Its form is... a Rodan!

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:40.250
Come in, 03! Status report!

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:40.940
It's huge!

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.110
Retreat!

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:31.280
The incomplete is to blame for all these unknowns

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:33.910
The incomplete is to blame for all these unknowns

00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:33.950
The i com l te i s

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:34.580
The incomplete is to blame for all these unknowns

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:37.700
They were all hack jobs, so let's perfect them

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:38.580
They were all hack jobs, so let's perfect them

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.050
We'll prove it one way or another

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:47.920
We have to go

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.720
We have to go

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:51.550
We have to make our move

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:53.430
We have to make our move

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:57.060
Right now we've got cold feet

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:59.810
But we'll fight for right

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:00.850
Not everything unanswered needs an answer

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:04.520
Not everything unanswered needs an answer

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:07.030
We decide what our future means, so stand up, honey

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:11.910
The more difficult it is, the more fun it gets

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:14.410
We decide what our future means, so stand up, honey

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:15.580
We have to be logical, I know

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:18.330
We have to be logical, I know

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:21.460
Yeah, I know that much

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:22.040
Let's oppose this crisis

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:26.630
Let's oppose this crisis

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:29.590
Let's oppose this crisis

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:30.340
Let's oppose this crisis

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:49.650
Singular Point—a place that
invalidates the laws of the world.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:53.400
It exists all over the Earth and produces red dust?

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:57.570
But that thingamajig can get rid of red dust.

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:01.580
<i>If</i> the Orthogonal Diagonalizer
can be completed, that is.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:04.830
Rodan can't survive without red dust.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:07.910
Even with the red dust gone,
the Singular Point that creates them will remain.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:10.090
I guess there's no easy way out.

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:13.840
On top of that, Godzilla in Tokyo is
quickly growing due to the Singular Point,

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.930
and we're heading toward a catastrophe.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:19.100
Longhorn Beetle thinks the
Catastrophe will destroy the universe.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:22.850
A gamma-ray burst? Diastrophism?
Gravitational collapse?

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:24.810
The downfall of humankind.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.530
We gotta stop it.

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:30.060
It's been four days since you
lost contact with Longhorn Beetle, huh?

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:34.150
Who are they to begin with?
Someone like us with nothing better to do?

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:38.700
They said someone called Ashihara predicted everything.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:44.790
The key figure of the Archetype research who roamed
around the world, his real identity still unknown.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:49.630
What's even more surprising is that the name of
this mansion's former owner is Michiyuki Ashihara.

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:53.590
Those are Singular Points?
Looks like a bunch of squiggly lines to me.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:57.720
This is what a 2-D drawing of a
higher-dimensional network looks like.

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:00.640
I think it was in here...

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:03.010
There!

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.390
Don't you remember?

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:09.100
Convert these sequences into
decimal numbers and reverse them.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.150
You mean the date embedded in the song?

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.020
Jet Jaguar, compare them.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:17.280
The embedded sequences
completely match the ones in the song.

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:21.600
Does this mean it was Ashihara who encrypted the song?

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:25.110
There's a crystal radio in here.

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:27.390
It was just receiving the song, not transmitting it?

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:31.290
It's natural to think that he was researching it just like us.

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:34.980
If it was in a memo left
by the owner who went missing, then...

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:38.590
it must have been embedded over 50 years ago!

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:41.300
Time machines are full of paradoxes.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.430
Like meeting yourself in the past.

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:45.310
Or killing an ancestor.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:49.810
However, one theory claims the
universe is rewritten after each time travel.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:54.320
If there's a paradox between the
past and the future, one of them changes.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:57.940
Wouldn't history keep changing and run amok?

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.400
You think so?

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:04.700
History would stop changing if we went
to a universe without a time machine.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:08.080
The same thing might happen
with a super-time calculation.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:14.090
If we send the result to the past,
the problem <i>would</i> be solved before it's entered.

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:19.840
Like digesting before eating. It wouldn't
be a problem if no info got transmitted.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:22.390
Transmitted without information...

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:24.300
Even if a signal is sent to the past,

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:27.600
there's no problem if it isn't recognized as information.

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:31.020
Let's try this. Go ahead and think of a number.

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:33.100
Nine.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:35.110
How many sunflowers over there?

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:37.980
Two, four, six...

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:38.900
Nine.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:43.320
What if your number was
sent there before you chose it?

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.740
Then forget nine—I choose three.

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.990
Alright, how many of those ornaments over there?

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:54.920
The information is received,
but there's nothing to indicate what it is.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:57.100
Then... minus one!

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:01.760
What if you send to the past info about
something that should exist but doesn't?

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:03.710
I see.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:06.640
Then, I'll go with that.

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:13.640
No dice, huh.

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:17.770
There is currently a serious global network failure.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:22.780
There are severed undersea cables, as well as
damaged power networks and base stations.

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:27.910
It's been 12 hours already...
And BB was the one who told <i>us </i>to hurry.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:31.870
Each country has a different concept of time.

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:35.790
I can't contact Upala. Is he here?

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:37.670
I haven't seen him yet.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.300
You should take a break.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:41.670
But...

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:43.670
Who's that?

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:45.930
Oh, no!

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:46.640
Pero 2!

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:47.760
Much appreciated!

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:51.270
You villain!

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:52.680
Got the better of me, huh?

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:55.600
Hey, hey, hey! Come on!

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.610
Let me out!

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:03.280
Are you Kamino Mei? The name's Lina.
Nice to meet you, I'm here in place of BB.

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:04.400
In his place?

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:09.370
He said he'd do the chitchat later since
he wants to focus on the experiment.

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:10.740
Seriously!?

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.750
Here, he told me to give this to you.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:18.290
Let's see. It's consistent with the information we have.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:19.670
Mr. Makita.

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:22.340
Okay. I'll take good care of it.

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:25.300
Alright! Mission accomplished.

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:28.680
Come, let's hurry!
We might get back in time for the experiment.

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:29.680
What?

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:31.680
We need to go now, or we'll miss it.

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:32.520
But...

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:34.180
I'll be off then.

00:07:34.730 --> 00:07:36.230
What's your name?

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:39.310
I'm Pero 2. Thank you for saving me there.

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:41.360
Are you good at cleaning?

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:43.940
I'm looking for a housekeeping
robot that can also translate.

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:45.040
Excuse me?

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:48.400
I'm going to the Japanese consulate in Kolkata.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:53.910
Send the data to everyone on the
list once the signals are back up.

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:58.080
I'm sure somebody will respond.
Thanks for everything.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:59.330
Be careful.

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:00.860
You too, Mr. Makita.

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:04.880
His daughter?

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:09.590
You better watch yourself around Dad.
He doesn't like people who are smarter than him.

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:10.970
It's a bit too late for that.

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:12.890
I knew it! He's hot under the collar.

00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:14.100
And so he sent you?

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:17.230
Nope. He's in a good mood when he's angry.

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:18.480
I don't get it.

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:22.110
If you don't have a license, I can drive for you.

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:24.980
It's okay. This car is tricky to control.

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:27.740
Going to SHIVA by land?

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:32.870
The cave is like a maze and we don't have
enough resources to cover each exit.

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:33.990
Where's BB?

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:38.750
He's playing with the calculator.
Can we really trust him?

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:44.880
How many supernatural phenomena experts
even exist in the world? We don't have the luxury.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:47.970
Godzilla has strong regenerative properties
on the outer layers of his skin.

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:50.260
And there's still that explosion...

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:54.010
There's a possibility that it'll cause
an even stronger explosion.

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:54.010
The government has decided on the attack.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:56.270
It must be eliminated as quickly as possible.

00:08:57.020 --> 00:09:00.900
They can't associate the explosion
with what happened to the streetlights.

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:04.120
It makes landfall, emits a gas, then burns to death.

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:06.780
And when it rose from the ashes,
rings appeared before its mouth.

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:10.280
You mean the laser beam that killed the giant Rodan?

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:14.580
We still can't find the Rodan carcass.
Just what is happening?

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:16.990
But we have to do something.

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:20.210
We've been a step behind all the way.

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:22.880
What should we do? How can we get ahead?

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:27.300
What do the other sequences mean?

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:30.300
Are they a description of what's going to happen?

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:35.390
Or maybe what to do when it happens?
Could it be a journal?

00:09:35.750 --> 00:09:39.890
Jet Jaguar, the hourly news at around 7:00 p.m. on July 6.

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:42.140
A blackout due to a power line malfunction.

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:45.610
Three drunk youths were rescued from a river.

00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:48.900
A senior citizen was rescued after
getting lost in the forest.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:49.940
What else?

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:55.530
Outaki Factory employees were
detained for breaking into Misakioku.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:58.350
Oh, that. Forget that part already!

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:02.080
Here it is.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:04.060
What is...?

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:05.760
"Solve it and it'll make sense."

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:06.840
"Solve it and it'll make sense"?

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:09.800
Yes. The MD hash for "Solve it and it'll make sense."

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:12.340
A code that can't be decoded without the answer.

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:23.350
is a match with the MD5 hash for
"Solve it and it'll make sense."

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:27.480
The quiz you sent to Longhorn Beetle? Why's that here?

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:32.650
MD5 hash was designed around 1990.

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:34.360
It didn't exist 50 years ago.

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:37.620
Is it predicting the future?

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:42.250
These sequences... are they somehow connected to us?

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:46.130
Jet Jaguar, what was Yun Arikawa doing at the time?

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:48.130
Talking to Misakioku.

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:50.630
It was a business call so it was recorded.

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:53.550
How'd you find that out?

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:55.840
How, you say...? The instructions said so.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:57.470
Instructions? From who?

00:10:57.470 --> 00:11:00.350
It's written right here, plain and simple.

00:10:59.140 --> 00:11:02.890
Instructions... plain and simple... written here...

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:05.230
Hey. Is any of this relevant?

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:10.520
What if these sequences are all an MD hash?

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:15.360
It's possible, but it's a code that
can't be decoded without an answer.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:17.530
But—I think decoding it is possible.

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:20.580
You mean with the supercomputer?

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:22.870
The first thing indicated was the time.

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:27.370
And that time referred to
"It's written right here, plain and simple."

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:31.340
The other hint is, "Solve it
and it'll make sense." And so...

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:36.630
If they're all MD hash, it's impossible
to restore the original sequences,

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:40.050
but that's not the case if this is indicating a time.

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:43.560
Narrowing it down to a date and time makes it possible...?

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:44.640
Jet Jaguar.

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:49.520
Reverse the date and time of the
past 100 years and the next 10 years

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:51.440
and calculate the MD5 hash.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:52.690
All right.

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:59.110
Each sequence is consistent
with the calculated MD hash values.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:05.330
It shows the time at 256 locations
for 41 days, starting July 6, 2030.

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:07.500
The order of incidents?

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:10.210
But it's not in order at all.

00:12:10.210 --> 00:12:12.290
Is there a meaning to how it's sorted?

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:15.710
What was I doing at the time?

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:16.920
Chatting.

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:17.970
Chatting?

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:22.970
Your chat with Longhorn Beetle
makes up 99.2 percent of the time.

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:24.470
Are you serious?

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:28.140
Okay. Read the chat in order of this list.

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:32.480
The government will soon
start Operation Exterminate Godzilla...

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:36.290
If the operation fails, we must abandon the Tokyo area.

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:36.290
Tokyo has already been met with enormous damage.

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:37.490
Even if we exterminate Godzilla...

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:39.740
The operation scheduled for today...

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:42.160
Aircrafts are taking
off from the base.

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:44.280
A deafening noise
from the fleet.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:46.570
This large battalion is...

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:47.500
The starting time of the
operation has been announced just now.

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:51.750
Those in restricted areas should evacuate immediately.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:57.380
Staying indoors may also not be safe.
Your lives may be in grave danger.

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:02.760
There you are.

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:06.270
Oh, you. I didn't think you were coming back.

00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:07.800
Bottled beer, please.

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:10.190
I put in a request for some days off.

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:11.980
Some chikuwabu and octopus, please.

00:13:11.980 --> 00:13:13.270
Coming right up.

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:16.030
I couldn't find my report anywhere.

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:22.320
I also contacted SHIVA consortium but
they didn't even remember its existence.

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:25.330
You're so diligent.

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:32.500
Years ago and out of the blue, a small fishing
village in Misakioku vanished from this world.

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:38.340
Ashihara, who was born in that village,
saw a giant creature emerge from the red sea.

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:41.510
The village was destroyed,
but the monster was eventually slain.

00:13:42.220 --> 00:13:47.280
Amidst the turmoil of war, the records were lost,
and people quickly forgot about the incident as well.

00:13:47.900 --> 00:13:51.810
But Ashihara found its
skeletal remains and bought the facility.

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:57.730
He noticed that it emitted
radio waves, and started monitoring them.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:01.240
After his death, its existence was forgotten.

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:04.950
All that remained was a manual on what
to do when the skeleton emits radio waves.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:07.410
Am I right so far?

00:14:08.520 --> 00:14:11.790
I said you're the type that only
makes more work for yourself.

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:16.420
Don't you think forgetting
could be a part of that work, too?

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:20.670
"When the fish is caught, the net is laid aside."

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:24.890
"To know what you know and
what you do not know is true knowledge."

00:14:24.890 --> 00:14:28.820
"If people have too much knowledge,
you'll have trouble ruling them."

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:33.460
Yes, it's me. Yes.

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:37.980
What? Understood. I'm on my way.

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:41.440
The alarm is ringing again.

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:44.150
"That is the Catastrophe."

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:45.070
"What is it?"

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:46.820
"The shape of the future? What time"

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:48.280
Emoji for calm down.

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:49.450
"Don't you have a problem right now?"

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:51.950
"Getting rid of red dust isn't enough."

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:52.910
"Anything."

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:53.830
"There must be a way."

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:54.750
"What time is it over there?"

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:56.210
"I think there's enough time."

00:14:56.210 --> 00:14:58.460
Send file 203001.jpg.

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:00.090
"Time goes "eep!" as it gets twisted."

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:01.800
"Send it to Tokyo?"

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:03.470
Emoji for flustered.

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:05.090
"Let's say it's possible for argument's sake."

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:06.550
"What do you think the future would look like?"

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:07.470
"...makes any calculation possible."

00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:10.140
"This is the answer."
"It's possible? Use the Catastrophe?"

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:12.310
"If we can use the bug."

00:15:12.310 --> 00:15:13.230
"That's even more amazing."

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:15.210
"It transcends the laws of physics, doesn't it?"

00:15:15.210 --> 00:15:16.060
"It bugged out?"

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:18.480
It kind of makes sense, and it doesn't...

00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:20.480
This is the prediction?

00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:22.650
No. Maybe it's a message.

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:23.610
From who?

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:25.980
"Tack on a Tokyo Sightseeing Flight, too."

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:26.360
"I'm in!"

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:27.450
"I'm surprised."

00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:28.570
"I could be nice."

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:30.330
"Thanks. Anyways, be careful."

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:31.290
"Good luck."

00:15:31.290 --> 00:15:32.740
Beep. That's it.

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:35.750
It sounds like two people
who are really hitting it off.

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:41.000
The message is snippets of your
conversations? Sent from the past?

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.300
Messages usually come from the past.

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:45.220
No, that's not what I mean.

00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:47.930
You were chatting at all points in time except twice.

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:49.010
Twice?

00:15:49.010 --> 00:15:52.390
Once, it was your phone call with Misakioku.

00:15:52.390 --> 00:15:55.730
Could the caller have been Longhorn Beetle?

00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:59.800
Wait a sec. That means Longhorn Beetle is Kamino.

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:00.770
Kamino Mei!

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:02.400
Kamino Mei?

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:06.030
The other instance occurs at a future time.

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:10.450
Exactly 9:30 a.m. on August 16, 2030.

00:16:10.450 --> 00:16:11.160
Four days from now?

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:15.200
If this message is made from
your conversations with Kamino...

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:20.420
Four days from now,
it'll be completed when she contacts me.

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:24.050
Or, am <i>I </i>going to contact her?

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:25.880
And then what'll happen?

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:27.630
I don't know.

00:16:34.850 --> 00:16:38.940
Misakioku... A skeleton in the basement
with a will of its own...

00:16:43.150 --> 00:16:44.230
This song...

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:47.820
You know it? It's a local lullaby.

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:52.410
It's a typical song about saying
goodbye or meeting someone new.

00:16:52.410 --> 00:16:54.080
Aren't those opposites?

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:58.710
Tributaries never become a river again.
A person who's lost never returns.

00:16:58.710 --> 00:17:01.000
Sounds to me like a permanent separation.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:04.170
But in the end, everything converges in the ocean.

00:17:06.050 --> 00:17:07.460
Red smoke?

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:08.510
Red dust!

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:11.220
Hey...

00:17:11.220 --> 00:17:12.510
My dad is over there!

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:17.020
Please drive safely!

00:17:17.020 --> 00:17:19.270
Oh, no. It's to the west.

00:17:19.270 --> 00:17:21.510
It's way off from the candidate.

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:22.400
How long will we take?

00:17:23.010 --> 00:17:24.440
Five more minutes.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:10.050
It's wreaking havoc.

00:18:10.050 --> 00:18:10.730
Get ready!

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:14.740
Front and center!

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:30.090
Don't waste it! Wait for the red dust to get thicker.

00:18:55.990 --> 00:18:57.240
Dad!

00:18:57.240 --> 00:18:59.200
What in the world are you doing here?

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:00.240
I brought her.

00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:06.080
We can't see Godzilla from here.
It's obscured by red dust.

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:09.880
We've been instructed to keep a safe distance.

00:19:10.800 --> 00:19:13.170
The time of the operation is drawing near.

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:16.760
Fighter planes are airborne.

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:23.100
Who would've imagined a scene
like this when Godzilla came ashore?

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:28.560
An explosion is sounding out!
The ground is shaking all the way here!

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:31.890
Did Godzilla get hit? I see flashes of light.

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:34.610
The thunderous noise continues.

00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:12.310
I woke up to your voice that painted my vision with color

00:22:12.310 --> 00:22:18.190
And it was the same shade of curiosity I find in my familiar daily life

00:22:18.190 --> 00:22:23.570
If this feeling can grow naturally on its own

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:29.450
Will it fall off one day like an unripe fruit, I wonder?

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:34.080
I don't know anything

00:22:34.080 --> 00:22:38.460
Not even anything about you

00:22:41.340 --> 00:22:46.970
Let me keep on dreaming for now

00:22:46.970 --> 00:22:51.350
If this moment is all I have now

00:22:51.810 --> 00:22:55.810
I can still feel the warmth in my palm

00:22:57.650 --> 00:23:03.070
My thrumming feelings open and burst out

00:23:03.070 --> 00:23:07.080
I want to keep learning more, like I am now

00:23:08.830 --> 00:23:13.620
This pulsating rhythm I feel just won't stop

00:23:13.620 --> 00:23:14.580
It won't stop
